.TH SMARTMKPACKAGENOTE 1 "2026-10-11" "smartmet-utils" "SmartMet Build Tools"
.SH NAME
smartmkpackagenote \- generate the SmartMet package identification ELF note
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smartmkpackagenote
.I output.o
.RI [ compiler ]
.br
.B smartmkpackagenote \-\-commit
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B smartmkpackagenote
writes an object file containing an ELF note with owner
.B SmartMet
and type
.BR 0x534d0001 ,
whose payload is a JSON object identifying the package being built:
.PP
.RS 4
{"type":"rpm","name":"smartmet-library-spine","version":"26.10.11-1.el8.fmi","commit":"0123456789ab"}
.RE
.PP
The shared SmartMet
.B makefile.inc
runs it in every directory containing a
.B smartmet\-*.spec
file and links the object into the libraries, engines, plugins and
programs built there. A running SmartMet Server reports the notes of all
loaded objects with the admin request
.BR what=packages ,
also on RHEL8 where rpmbuild does not add the freedesktop.org
.B .note.package
note, and for builds made outside rpmbuild.
.PP
Inside rpmbuild the
.B type
is
.B rpm
and the name and version come from the
.BR RPM_PACKAGE_NAME ,
.B RPM_PACKAGE_VERSION
and
.B RPM_PACKAGE_RELEASE
environment variables. Otherwise the
.B type
is
.BR source ,
the name is that of the spec file and the version is read from its
.B Version
and
.B Release
fields, with
.B %{?dist}
expanded by
.B rpm \-\-eval
when available.
.PP
The
.B commit
is taken from the
.B SMARTMET_GIT_COMMIT
environment variable when it is set, which
.B makefile.inc
does in the git checkout so that the value survives into rpmbuild. Otherwise
it is resolved with git, provided the
.B Makefile
of the current directory is tracked. A
.B \-dirty
suffix marks uncommitted changes to tracked files.
.PP
On x86_64 the object also declares the IBT and SHSTK CET features, since
the linker would otherwise disable CET in every binary the object is
linked into.
.PP
The output file is left untouched if its contents would not change, and it
is removed if the directory has no spec file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-commit
Print the git commit of the current directory, with a
.B \-dirty
suffix if needed, and exit. Prints nothing outside a git checkout.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CC
Compiler used to assemble the note if none is given on the command line
(default
.BR gcc ).
.TP
.B SMARTMET_GIT_COMMIT
Commit to embed instead of querying git. An empty value omits the commit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smartbuildcfg (1),
.BR readelf (1)
